<article class="env-corollary" id="039T">
<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/039T">Corollary <span data-tag="039T">7.3.5.3</span>.</a> Let $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$ be a category, let $\mathscr {G}: \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}\rightarrow \operatorname{Set_{\Delta }}$ be a diagram of simplicial sets, let $\operatorname{\mathcal{D}}$ be an $\infty $-category, and let $F_0:  \underset { \longrightarrow }{\mathrm{holim}}( \mathscr {G} ) \rightarrow \operatorname{\mathcal{D}}$ be a diagram. The following conditions are equivalent: </p>
<p><dl>
<dt>$(1)$</dt>
<dd><p>
The diagram $F_0$ admits a left Kan extension along the projection map $U:  \underset { \longrightarrow }{\mathrm{holim}}( \mathscr {G} ) \rightarrow \operatorname{N}_{\bullet }(\operatorname{\mathcal{C}})$. 
</p>
</dd>
<dt>$(2)$</dt>
<dd><p>
For every object $C \in \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$, the diagram 
</p>
<div class="equation">
  \[  \mathscr {G}(C) \simeq \{ C\}  \times _{ \operatorname{N}_{\bullet }(\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}) }  \underset { \longrightarrow }{\mathrm{holim}}( \mathscr {G} ) \hookrightarrow  \underset { \longrightarrow }{\mathrm{holim}}( \mathscr {G} ) \xrightarrow {F_0} \operatorname{\mathcal{D}} \]
</div>
<p>
 admits a colimit in the $\infty $-category $\operatorname{\mathcal{D}}$. 
</p>
</dd>
</dl></p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
<p>
<strong>Proof.</strong>
      For each object $C \in \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$, the inclusion map 
    <p>
<div class="equation">
  \[  \mathscr {G}(C) \hookrightarrow \operatorname{N}_{\bullet }( \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}_{/C} ) \times _{ \operatorname{N}_{\bullet }(\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}) }  \underset { \longrightarrow }{\mathrm{holim}}(\mathscr {G} ) \simeq  \underset { \longrightarrow }{\mathrm{holim}}( \mathscr {G}|_{ \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}_{/C} } ) \]
</div>
<p>
       is right anodyne (Example <a data-tag="039E" href="/tag/039E">5.3.6.4</a>), and therefore right cofinal. The desired result now follows by combining Proposition <a data-tag="0300" href="/tag/0300">7.3.5.1</a> with Corollary <a data-tag="02NS" href="/tag/02NS">7.2.2.10</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
</p>
</p></p></article>
